    <heading level="1">Section 1.2 Exercises</heading>
    <heading level="1">Practice Makes Perfect</heading>
    <paragraph>Simplify Expressions with Absolute Value</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, fill in $$&lt; , &gt; ,$$ or $$=$$ for each of the following pairs of numbers.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="59" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$|-7| \text{\_\_\_} - |-7|$$ ⓑ $$6 \text{\_\_\_} - |-6|$$ ⓒ $$|-11| \text{\_\_\_} - 11$$ ⓓ $$-(-13) \text{\_\_\_} - |-13|$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$&gt;&gt;$$ ⓑ $$&gt;&gt;$$ ⓒ $$&gt;&gt;$$ ⓓ $$&gt;&gt;$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="60" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$-|-9| \text{\_\_\_} |-9|$$ ⓑ $$-8 \text{\_\_\_} |-8|$$ ⓒ $$|-1| \text{\_\_\_} - 1$$ ⓓ $$-(-14) \text{\_\_\_} - |-14|$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="61" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$-|2| \text{\_\_\_} - |-2|$$ ⓑ $$-12 \text{\_\_\_} - |-12|$$ ⓒ $$|-3| \text{\_\_\_} - 3$$ ⓓ $$|-19| \text{\_\_\_} - (-19)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$==$$ ⓑ $$==$$ ⓒ $$&gt;&gt;$$ ⓓ $$==$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="62" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$-|-4| \text{\_\_\_} - |4|$$ ⓑ $$5 \text{\_\_\_} - |-5|$$ ⓒ $$-|-10| \text{\_\_\_} - 10$$ ⓓ $$-|-0| \text{\_\_\_} - (-0)$$</paragraph>
